Subject: [PATCH] Mobile map fixes + react-hooks/set-state-in-effect refactor

One file changed: src/components/map-reference-section.tsx

Mobile map fixes:
  - Responsive map height (h-[320px] sm:h-[380px] md:h-[460px] w-full max-w-full),
    replacing the fixed inline style={{ height: 420 }}.
  - Touch hover-follow disabled: isTouchRef detects a coarse pointer; the map
    `mousemove` preview line never updates on touch, so nothing follows the
    finger. Plot points are still committed on tap/click only.
  - Overlay toolbars (draw toolbar + base-layer switcher) are width-capped and
    the switcher wraps on mobile so they never overflow a narrow map.

Lint fixes (react-hooks/set-state-in-effect, react-hooks v7):
  - talukas loader, villages loader, boundary loader: all setState moved inside
    an async IIFE guarded by `cancelled` (also fixes a stale-fetch race).
  - draw-reset effect: guarded with prevVillageIdRef so the reset is conditional.
  - language relabel effect: setForm deferred into a microtask with a guard.

Behavior unchanged. No village data, shapefile, or GIS files touched.

